><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">63</td><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">565</td><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">1.0</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">Ref</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;Yes</td><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">8</td><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">2</td><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">4.4</td><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">(0.9&#x02013;2.2)</td><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">2</td><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">2</td><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">11.7</td><td align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">(1.3&#x02013;108.5)</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tbfnote2"><label>a</label><p>Adjusted for stratification variables (gender, age at diagnosis, region of residence at diagnosis).</p></fn><fn id="tbfnote3"><label>b</label><p>s.d.&#x0003d;standard deviation.</p></fn><fn id="tbfnote4"><label>c</label><p>X&#x0003d;missing values.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap>).</p><p>A statistically significant association between birth order and childhood ALL was observed (<italic>P</italic>-trend&#x0003d;0.07&#x02013;OR&#x0003d;2.0; CI (3.1&#x02013;3.7) for children born fourth). A similar association was observed with AML.</p><p>No association between breast-feeding, irrespective of its duration, and childhood AL was observed (<xref rid="tbl3" ref-type="table">Table 3</xref> <table-wrap id="tbl3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Association between childhood acute leukaemia and breast-feeding (analysis restricted to children older than 1 year)</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="center" char="."/><col align="center" char="."/><col align="center" 